  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Consultancy costs - Health basket</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Konsultkostnader - H&#xE4;lsobasket</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xF6;det g&#xE4;ller konsultkostnader till Belgian Development Agency i Uganda (BTC Uganda). BTC har utf&#xF6;rt en studie f&#xF6;r en givargemensam h&#xE4;lsobasket i Uganda, ett st&#xF6;d som planeras p&#xE5;b&#xF6;rjas under 2016. H&#xE4;lsobasketen kommer anv&#xE4;ndas f&#xF6;r att st&#xE4;rka h&#xE4;lsotj&#xE4;nster p&#xE5; distriktniv&#xE5; i landet. Sverige planerade initialt att samfinansiera den &#xE4;nnu ej uppr&#xE4;ttade h&#xE4;lsobasketen, men kommer ist&#xE4;llet sannolikt ing&#xE5; ett liknande st&#xF6;d som implementeras av V&#xE4;rldsbanken, d&#xE5; detta bed&#xF6;ms vara ett b&#xE4;ttre alternativ.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This support relates to consultancy costs for the Belgian Development Agency in Uganda (BTC Uganda). BTC has carried out a study for a new Health Basket Fund in Uganda, planned to be rolled out during 2016. The Health Basket will be used to strengthen health services on district level in the country. Sweden had initially planned to co-finance the Health Basket, but will now most likely fund a similar contribution implemented by the World Bank, as this is assessed to be a better alternative.</narrative>
  </description>
